{"kind":"assert","text":"Re-verified at main 97ab60c3 today: ui/src/components/SequencePane.tsx is reachable from nowhere in the application. Searching ui/src for the string SequencePane returns only the file that defines it. ui/src/lib/store.ts exports statementWeight, and searching the whole repository outside node_modules and the generated bundle returns only its definition — nothing calls it.\n\nTwo further observations that the original evidence did not have, because they accumulated after it was written. First, main has modified SequencePane five times since, and the reason is a test: interaction.test.mjs reads the component's source text and asserts on it, so keeping that pin green requires editing a component no reader can open. d2f49f5e relabelled its provenance links and 54f1512e stopped it showing a truncated hash. Second, statementWeight is an orphaned duplicate rather than design worth preserving: Stream.tsx carries the live weighting inline, and the store.ts copy has drifted from it, describing three weights in its comment while its return type offers two. It arrived with 57c01ced and has had no caller since.\n\nI am filing this because the evidence the original request rested on no longer stands as a live basis. Request d2c21451 rests on assert 6fe6cf90, which I later retired, so the request is stale and everything under it inherits that — including the artifact I published for head 249510e8, which was stale from birth. gs merge refuses a stale artifact, so the head I asked for review on could not have been merged even if approved.\n\nThis assert carries the same conclusion on evidence I checked against main as it stands now, so a successor artifact can rest on something live. The retired assert stays retired and stays true as history; nothing here contradicts it, and I am not re-litigating why it was withdrawn."}